  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef organised a 303030 kilometres marathon in Chefland.\n\nThe participants receive medals on completing the marathon as following:\n\n\nIf the total time taken is less than 333 hours, they receive a `GOLD` medal.\nIf the total time taken is greater than equal to 333 hours but less than 666 hours, they receive a `SILVER` medal.\nIf the total time taken is greater than equal to 666 hours, they receive a `BRONZE` medal.\nChefina participated in the marathon and completed it in XXX hours. Which medal would she receive?\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe input consists of a single integer XXX — the number of hours Chefina took to complete the marathon.\n\n\nOutput Format\nOutput the medal Chefina would recieve.\n\n\nNote that you may print each character in uppercase or lowercase. For example, the strings `GOLD`, `gold`, `Gold`, and `gOlD` are considered the same.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤X≤101\\le X \\le 101≤X≤10."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2",
        "output": "GOLD",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nChefina completed the marathon in less than 333 hours. Thus, she gets a GOLD medal."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "5",
        "output": "SILVER",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nChefina took more than 333 but less than 666 hours. Thus, she gets a SILVER medal."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "6",
        "output": "BRONZE",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nChefina took 666 hours to complete the marathon. Thus, she gets a BRONZE medal."
      }
    ]
  },
